              "type": "text",
              "content": "96"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.783,
            0.105,
            0.899,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.147,
            0.546,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. In Fig. 6.36, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { Q R } } { \\mathrm { Q S } } = \\frac { \\mathrm { Q T } } { \\mathrm { P R } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 1 = \\angle 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " .Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\operatorname { P Q S } \\sim \\Delta"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " TQR."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.221,
            0.548,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. S and T are points on sides PR and QR of ∆ PQR such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{P} = \\angle \\mathrm{RTS}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { R P Q } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { R T S }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.294,
            0.546,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. In Fig. 6.37, if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\; \\mathrm { A B E } \\cong \\Delta \\; \\mathrm { A C D }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  ADE  \\sim \\Delta  ABC"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.349,
            0.516,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. In Fig. 6.38, altitudes AD and CE of ∆ ABC intersect each other at the point P. Show that:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.411,
            0.328,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  AEP  \\sim \\Delta  CDP"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.437,
            0.336,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  ABD  \\sim \\Delta  CBE"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.463,
            0.339,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  AEP  \\sim \\Delta  ADB"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.489,
            0.338,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { P D C } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { B E C }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.517,
            0.517,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. E is a point on the side AD produced of a parallelogram ABCD and BE intersects CD at F. Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B E } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { C F B }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.59,
            0.515,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. In Fig. 6.39, ABC and AMP are two right triangles, right angled at B and M respectively. Prove that:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.649,
            0.338,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  ABC  \\sim \\Delta  AMP"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.679,
            0.295,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { C A } } { \\mathrm { P A } }   =   \\frac { \\mathrm { B C } } { \\mathrm { M P } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.725,
            0.517,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. CD and GH are respectively the bisectors of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle ACB   and   \\angle EGF"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that D and H lie on sides AB and FE of ∆ ABC and ∆ EFG respectively. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{If} \\Delta \\mathrm{ABC} \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm{FEG}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " show that: (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { C D } } { \\mathrm { G H } } = \\frac { \\mathrm { A C } } { \\mathrm { F G } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  DCB  \\sim \\Delta  HGE"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { D C A }   \\sim   \\Delta \\mathrm { H G F }"
            }
          ]
        },
